invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_avx2_number.h
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_avx2_number
reason: value_at_or_zero reads values[count], one word past the count, so
  words_to_digits reads one word past the k words of the modulus, of
  digit_r2 and of the base when it fills the top digits. The arrays the
  tests pass are larger than k words, so their bytes hold and every test
  passes. rsa_avx2_number runs words_to_digits over a heap object of
  exactly k words, at every word count, and fails on the read.

--- old
    return index < count ? values[index] : 0;
--- new
    return index <= count ? values[index] : 0;
